    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nLet XPU use the existing Model Runner V2 path that reuses GDN attention metadata across KV cache groups (#58762). Both the reuse path and the aligned state index precompute it depends on in mamba `align` mode were limited to CUDA; this PR allows XPU in both checks.\n\n## Claims\n\n- On XPU, hybrid GDN models (Qwen3.5 / Qwen3.6 family) build GDN metadata once per KV cache spec per step and re-gather state indices for the other groups via `update_block_table()`, as on CUDA. With 3 GDN KV cache groups, 2 of 3 metadata builds per step are replaced.\n- Outputs are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nIntel Arc Pro B70, MTP with `num_speculative_tokens=3`, eager mode, prefix caching on (mamba `align` mode), greedy decoding with `logprobs=1`. GDN metadata calls were counted inside the workers; baseline is unmodified main.\n\n| Model | Config | GDN `build()` calls (baseline → this PR) | `update_block_table()` calls | Outputs |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Qwen3.5-0.8B | TP=1, bf16, B1+B8 | 819 → 273 | 0 → 546 | tokens and logprobs identical across 5 processes |\n| Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 | TP=2, B1+B8, per worker | 2133 → 711 | 0 → 1422 | tokens identical across 4 processes; B8 logprobs identical; B1 max logprob difference 0.093, baseline-vs-baseline 0.075 |\n\nThroughput on Qwen3.5-0.8B (128 input / 64 output tokens, median of 5 runs per process, A-B-B-A process order):\n\n| Batch | Baseline (A1 / A2) | This PR (B1 / B2) | Paired change |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 183.5 / 181.1 tok/s | 189.4 / 192.1 tok/s | +3.2% / +6.1% |\n| 8 | 1329.9 / 1342.0 tok/s | 1404.9 / 1399.1 tok/s | +5.7% / +4.3% |\n\nRun-to-run variation within a process was up to 5%. On Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 the throughput difference was within run-to-run noise.\n\n```bash\npytest tests/v1/attention/test_gdn_metadata_builder.py tests/v1/worker/test_mamba_utils.py\n# 70 passed, 36 skipped (existing CUDA-only cases)\n```\n\nChanged-file pre-commit (including mypy) passed.\n\n## Details\n\n`GDNAttentionMetadataBuilder.supports_update_block_table` required `device.type == \"cuda\"`. In mamba `align` mode, `update_block_table()` reads the indices produced by `MambaSpecDecodeGPUContext.compute_aligned_state_indices()`, which asserted `seq_lens.is_cuda`. Qwen3.5 uses `align` mode by default when prefix caching is enabled, so allowing XPU only in the first check fails at that assert. The precompute is a Triton kernel and runs unchanged on XPU; identical outputs above confirm the indices match the per-group build.\n\nNo new test is added: the existing builder tests that cover `update_block_table()` are device-independent and pass, and there is no existing unit test for the precompute numerics; the change only widens two device checks, and the end-to-end comparison above exercises both on XPU.\n\n#58851 moves this sharing into the builder and drops the CUDA check for sharing itself, but keeps the aligned-index precompute CUDA-only. This PR is independent of it; the `compute_aligned_state_indices()` change is still needed for XPU in `align` mode either way.\n\nLimitations: XPU only (no CUDA behavior change), eager mode only; graph mode was not exercised.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
